    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133) across the application:\n\n**New logic** \u2014 `membershipLevel` starts at 1, adds 1 when an email is present, adds 1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, and is capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure). This drops the old household-size-driven `GOLD`/`SILVER`/`BRONZE` behavior.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n- **`mapper/MembershipLevel.java`** (new) \u2014 a shared static helper `forOwner(Owner)` computing the level, mirroring the existing `OwnerLocality` helper style, so the mapper and controller derive it identically.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` MapStruct expression with a `membershipLevel` mapping delegating to `MembershipLevel.forOwner`.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` (string) response schema with `membershipLevel` (integer, min 1, max 3, read-only). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the new field and removes the old one.\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` instead of no tier, added the import, and I cleaned up a stale javadoc that referenced the retired `GOLD` tier.\n\nThe acceptance test's `coreNumericLevel` (expecting `membershipLevel` = 3 for a unique-named owner with an email) passes, and the audit log confirms `owner created ... membershipLevel=3`.",
